Wireless Attacks
-----------------

    Wireless Deauthentication Attacks
        - Disconnects a person from the wifi
    
    Protecting against deauth Attacks
    --------------------------------
        - IEEE has already addressd the problem
            - updates included with 802.11ac
            - some important management frames are encrypted 
                - Disassociate,deauthenticate,channel switch announcements,
                have been hidden via encryption.
            - Not everything is encrypted though..
                    beacons,probes,authenticaition,
    
    Radio frequency (RF) jamming
    -------------------------
        -type of DoS that effects all people
        
        - transmit interfering wireless signal
            -Decrease the signal-to-noise ratio at the receiving device
            - the receiving device can't hear the good signal

        - Sometimes not intentional
            - interference,not jamming
            - microwave oven,florecent lights

        - Jamming is intentional though..

        Ways to jam:
            - sending legitimate constant,random bits through the network
            - Data send at random times - random data and legitimate frames
            - reactive jammming - only when somone else tries to communicate

            - needs to be somewhere close

            - time to go fox hunting
                - directional antenna


                
        
    
